{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfc76rwBsX5eaqa754ZJB", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If every merge to main ships automatically, there is no separate release step. Merging the PR to main is the release.\n\n- **Cutting a release:** merge your change to main. Don't push a `vYYYY.MM.N` tag, because tags no longer trigger anything.\n- **Before you merge:** treat the merge as a production deploy. Make sure tests pass and the PR is reviewed.\n- **Rolling back:** revert the commit on main, and the revert ships the same way.\n- **Publishing by hand:** don't. The old rule against it probably still holds.\n\nThe repo has no CI or workflow files, so I couldn't confirm the pipeline. The details live wherever your CI is configured, and I don't know how it handles things like versioning, changelogs or deploy gates.\n\nI found an EngramDB memory saying releases are cut by pushing a `vYYYY.MM.N` tag. I marked it as challenged, using your statement as the evidence. I didn't rewrite it, since I don't know the new process well enough to describe it. If you tell me how it works, including any version or changelog handling, I can record that and replace the old convention."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 524, "cache_read_input_tokens": 26159, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 524}, "output_tokens": 361, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "60f0c5e2-db3d-4f17-8683-0ceb41cf61e1", "uuid": "8319889e-5b70-48b6-a59b-03edb9054006", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T19:56:17.351Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfc76rbMzUdvg1TE1VD9y"}
